* Simplified behavioural NE555, written for circuit-tutor (not the vendor model).
* Comparators at VCC/3 (TRIG) and the CTRL voltage, nominally 2*VCC/3 (THR); TRIG wins
* over THR as in the real part; RESET below 0.7 V forces the output low.
* The latch is a 1 nF capacitor on node q, clamped near 0..1 V; q > 0.5 means "set".
* Pin order matches the registry line: gnd trig out reset ctrl thr dis vcc
.subckt NE555 gnd trig out reset ctrl thr dis vcc
r1 vcc ctrl 5k
r2 ctrl lo 5k
r3 lo gnd 5k
bq 0 q i = 1m * (u(v(lo) - v(trig)) - u(v(thr) - v(ctrl)) * u(v(trig) - v(lo)) - 2 * u(0.7 - v(reset, gnd)))
cq q 0 1n
vhi hi 0 1
dhi q hi dclamp
dlo 0 q dclamp
bout o1 gnd v = u(v(q) - 0.5) * u(v(reset, gnd) - 0.7) * max(v(vcc, gnd) - 1.7, 0)
rout o1 out 10
* discharge transistor: about 10 ohm to GND while the latch is reset
bdis dis gnd i = (1 - u(v(q) - 0.5)) * v(dis, gnd) / 10
rq vcc gnd 1.5k
.model dclamp d(is=1e-14)
.ends NE555
